Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:40:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/tu: aggressive LRZ early-depth test retention on A7xx

Hardware Low-Resolution Z (LRZ) on Adreno 7xx enables hardware early-depth
rejection before fragment shading. Default Turnip disables LRZ under
conservative conditions (e.g. blend states or sample mask variations).

On Adreno 735 (POCO F6), disabling LRZ wastes ALU cycles on occluded pixels.
This patch prevents premature LRZ disabling and keeps early depth testing
active across dynamic depth state transitions.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc
index a98f123..b4512e0 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc
@@ -210,6 +210,20 @@ tu_lrz_disable_during_render_pass(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd)
    if (!cmd->state.lrz.valid)
       return;
 
+   /* Adreno 735 / A7xx optimization:
+    * Do not aggressively disable LRZ on transient depth write toggles.
+    * Keep the existing depth bounds valid if the depth test remains enabled.
+    */
+   if (cmd->device->physical_device->info->chip >= 7) {
+      if (cmd->state.depth_test_enable) {
+         /* Retain LRZ fastpath for occlusion queries and depth pre-passes */
+         cmd->state.lrz.fast_clear = true;
+         return;
+      }
+   }
+
    cmd->state.lrz.valid = false;
 }
 
